polyoMatrix -- Matrix attached to a collection of cells
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        polyoMatrix Q
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a collection of cells
  * Outputs:
      * the matrix attached to the collection of cells encoded by Q.

Description
===========

Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a collection of cells and $[(a,b),(c,d)]$ be the smallest
interval of $\ZZ^2$ containing $\mathcal{P}$. The matrix $M(\mathcal{P})$ is a
matrix having $d-b+1$ rows and $c-a+1$ columns with
$M(\mathcal{P})_{i,j}=x_{(i,j)}$ if $(i,j)$ is a vertex of $\mathcal{P}$,
otherwise it is zero.
This routine returns the matrix of the collection of cells encoded by Q. In the
following example we assume for simplicity that the smallest interval
containing $\mathcal{P}$ is $[(1,1),(c,d)]$, with $c,d>1$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = cellCollection {{1,1}, {2,1}, {2,2}}                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = {{1, 1}, {2, 1}, {2, 2}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : CollectionOfCells                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = polyoMatrix Q                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | 0       x_(2,3) x_(3,3) |                                             |
|     | x_(1,2) x_(2,2) x_(3,2) |                                             |
|     | x_(1,1) x_(2,1) x_(3,1) |                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                3            |
|o2 : Matrix (QQ[x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   ])  <--        |
|                 3,3   3,2   3,1   2,3   2,2   2,1   1,2   1,1               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                    3                        |
|(QQ[x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   ])                         |
|     3,3   3,2   3,1   2,3   2,2   2,1   1,2   1,1                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = cellCollection {{1, 3}, {2, 2}, {3, 1}, {2, 4}, {3, 5}, {4, 4}, {5, |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3}, {4, 2}, {6, 4}, {5, 1}, {7, 5}, {7, 1}, {4, 6}, {5, 7}, {6, 6}};         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = polyoMatrix Q                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | 0       0       0       0       x_(5,8) x_(6,8) 0       0       |     |
|     | 0       0       0       x_(4,7) x_(5,7) x_(6,7) x_(7,7) 0       |     |
|     | 0       0       x_(3,6) x_(4,6) x_(5,6) x_(6,6) x_(7,6) x_(8,6) |     |
|     | 0       x_(2,5) x_(3,5) x_(4,5) x_(5,5) x_(6,5) x_(7,5) x_(8,5) |     |
|     | x_(1,4) x_(2,4) x_(3,4) x_(4,4) x_(5,4) x_(6,4) x_(7,4) 0       |     |
|     | x_(1,3) x_(2,3) x_(3,3) x_(4,3) x_(5,3) x_(6,3) 0       0       |     |
|     | 0       x_(2,2) x_(3,2) x_(4,2) x_(5,2) x_(6,2) x_(7,2) x_(8,2) |     |
|     | 0       0       x_(3,1) x_(4,1) x_(5,1) x_(6,1) x_(7,1) x_(8,1) |     |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Matrix (QQ[x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   , x   ,  |
|                 8,6   8,5   8,2   8,1   7,7   7,6   7,5   7,4   7,2   7,1   |
