innerInterval -- Inner interval of a collection of cells
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        innerInterval(a, b, Q)
  * Inputs:
      * a, a list of two integers representing a point in $\mathbb{Z}^2$
      * b, a list of two integers representing a point in $\mathbb{Z}^2$
      * Q, a collection of cells
  * Outputs:
      * true if $[a,b]$ is an inner interval of Q, and false otherwise

Description
===========

Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a collection of cells. An interval $[a,b] \subseteq
\mathbb{Z}^2$ is called an inner interval of $\mathcal{P}$ if every cell
contained in $[a,b]$ also belongs to $\mathcal{P}$. This function returns true
if $[a,b]$ is an inner interval of $\mathcal{P}$, and false otherwise.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = cellCollection {{1,1}, {1,2}, {2,1}, {2,3}};|
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : innerInterval({1,1}, {3,3}, Q)                  |
|                                                     |
|o2 = false                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : innerInterval({1,1}, {3,2}, Q)                  |
|                                                     |
|o3 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

