collectionIsConnected -- Check if a collection of cells is connected
********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        collectionIsConnected Q
  * Inputs:
      * Q, a collection of cells
  * Outputs:
      * a sequence. The first component is a Boolean value: true if Q is
        connected, otherwise false. The second component gives the number of
        connected components of the collection of cells.

Description
===========

A collection of cells $\mathcal{P}$ is connected if for every pair of cells $A$
and $B$ of $\mathcal{P}$ there exists a path of cells $A=C_1,...,C_t=B$ of
$\mathcal{P}$, such that $C_i\cap C_{i+1}$ is an edge, for all $i=1,..,t-1$.
This function determines whether the collection of cells $\mathcal{P}$ is
connected and the number of the connected components.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = cellCollection {{1,1},{2,1},{3,2}};|
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : collectionIsConnected Q                |
|                                            |
|o2 = (false, 2)                             |
|                                            |
|o2 : Sequence                               |
+--------------------------------------------+

